>> title: Tandoori Marinade
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: indian, yogurt, chicken, marinade, grill
>> servings: 6
>> time: 15 min
>> step.1: whisk to a paste
>> step.2: grate in
>> step.3: whisk in
>> step.4: beat in, marinate 4 to 8 hr

Whisk @Kashmiri chile powder{1%Tbs}, @ground turmeric{1/2%tsp}, @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @ground coriander{1%tsp}, and @garam masala{1%tsp} with @lemon juice{2%Tbs}(30 mL) to a loose paste.

Grate @garlic{4%cloves} and @fresh ginger{1%Tbs} into @&(~1)spice paste{}.

Whisk @&(~1)paste{} into @thick yogurt{1%cup}(240 g; Greek or hung curd) with @kosher salt{2%tsp}.

Beat @mustard oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) and @dried fenugreek leaves{1%tsp}(kasuri methi, crushed) into @&(~1)marinade{}, then coat 2 lb of slashed chicken and chill it 4 to 8 hours.
